endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (In February 2026, the programme strengthened adolescent and youth access to quality sexual and reproductive health \(SRH\) services across Damboa, Mafa, Girei and Fufore LGAs of Borno and Adamawa states through targeted commodity distribution, supportive supervision, and service delivery.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Essential SRH commodities were successfully distributed to Gurin and Girei PHCCs, improving the availability of critical supplies and enhancing the quality of care for adolescents and young people. Supportive supervision was also conducted across Malabu, Girei B, and Gurin PHCCs to ensure adherence to clinical standards and the provision of appropriate, youth-friendly services.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Across PHC facilities of Simari, Alkalari, Girei B, Malabu, Ribadu, Jabbi Lamba, and Gurin adolescents and youths accessed a wide range of services, including antenatal care, safe deliveries and postnatal care, family planning, STI treatment, and counseling. These services were delivered by trained healthcare providers under the Adolescent and Youth Friendly Health Services \(AYFHS\) approach, ensuring a safe, confidential, and supportive environment.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (The intervention recorded strong service uptake, particularly in antenatal care, STI treatment, family planning, and counseling, demonstrating increased awareness and utilization of available services among adolescents and young people reaching about 2985 \(2417 female and 568 male\) participants across communities.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Overall, the integrated approach significantly improved access to quality SRH services, strengthened health system responsiveness, and contributed to better health outcomes and wellbeing for adolescents and youths across the targeted communities.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
